            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery bypass graft surgery during heart transplantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>224-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/icvts/ivs432</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a patient who was submitted to coronary artery bypass graft surgery (CABG) during heart transplant as, during bench exploration, the donor heart presented a palpable atherosclerotic lesion in the anterior descending artery, not detected before harvesting. The patent internal thoracic artery from a previous CABG was used.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
